            <h4>FAQ</h4>
            <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          </div>
        </div><%// section-heading %>
        <div purpose="faq">
          <div purpose="accordion">
            <div purpose="accordion-body">
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="jamf-faq__header1" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#jamf-faq__body1" aria-controls="jamf-faq__body1">
                  Does Fleet replace Jamf?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="jamf-faq__body1" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="jamf-faq__header1">
                  Yes. Fleet manages Macs, iPhones, and iPads with Apple’s MDM and declarative device management, and manages Windows, Linux, and Android from the same place. Many teams replace Jamf and the second tool they use for everything else. See <a href="/apple">Apple device management with Fleet</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="jamf-faq__header2" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#jamf-faq__body2" aria-controls="jamf-faq__body2">
                  Can I move Macs from Jamf without wiping them?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="jamf-faq__body2" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="jamf-faq__header2">
                  Yes. Apple’s built-in migration moves devices to Fleet without a wipe. Teams usually run Fleet alongside Jamf for a pilot group, then migrate by department or location. See the <a href="/articles/mac-admins-guide-to-switching-from-jamf-to-fleet">Mac admin’s guide to switching from Jamf</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="jamf-faq__header3" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#jamf-faq__body3" aria-controls="jamf-faq__body3">
                  Does Fleet help with the migration?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="jamf-faq__body3" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="jamf-faq__header3">
                  Yes. Fleet offers free migration services and dedicated support for teams switching from Jamf. See <a href="/articles/free-migration-from-jamf-to-fleet">free migration from Jamf to Fleet</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="jamf-faq__header4" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#jamf-faq__body4" aria-controls="jamf-faq__body4">
                  How do Jamf concepts map to Fleet?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="jamf-faq__body4" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="jamf-faq__header4">
                  Configuration profiles, Smart Groups, extension attributes, and policies all have Fleet equivalents. See <a href="/articles/translating-jamf-pro-terminology">translating Jamf Pro terminology</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="jamf-faq__header5" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#jamf-faq__body5" aria-controls="jamf-faq__body5">
                  Which Apple platforms does Fleet support?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="jamf-faq__body5" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="jamf-faq__header5">
                  macOS, iOS, and iPadOS. iOS and iPadOS are supported only with MDM turned on. To learn more, check out the <a href="/docs/get-started/faq#what-host-operating-systems-does-fleet-support">supported OS versions</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="jamf-faq__header6" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#jamf-faq__body6" aria-controls="jamf-faq__body6">
                  Can Fleet manage Windows and Linux too?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="jamf-faq__body6" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="jamf-faq__header6">
                  Yes. Fleet manages <a href="/windows">Windows</a> and <a href="/linux">Linux</a> with the same AI-native workflow, policies, and reports as your Macs. New Windows PCs can arrive ready to use with zero touch and no Microsoft license.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="jamf-faq__header7" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#jamf-faq__body7" aria-controls="jamf-faq__body7">
                  Can Fleet work with Munki, Puppet, or Chef?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="jamf-faq__body7" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="jamf-faq__header7">
                  Yes, via a bootstrap package. To learn more, check out the <a href="/guides/setup-experience#bootstrap-package">setup experience guide</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="jamf-faq__header8" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#jamf-faq__body8" aria-controls="jamf-faq__body8">
                  Is Fleet open source?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="jamf-faq__body8" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="jamf-faq__header8">
                  Yes. The majority of Fleet is released under the MIT license, and all of Fleet’s source code is public on GitHub at <a href="https://github.com/fleetdm/fleet" target="_blank">github.com/fleetdm/fleet</a>. You can self-host Fleet or use Fleet cloud, with every feature either way. See the <a href="/lp/open-source">open source MDM page</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p purpose="contact-note">Have another question? <a href="/docs/get-started/faq">Read the full FAQ</a> or <a href="/contact">talk to an engineer</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
